Description: VP8 with LibWebRTC's own encoder, not GStreamer's vp8enc
 With the LibWebRTC backend on the GLib ports, WebKit encodes VP8 through its GStreamer encoder element (vp8enc). On
 WPE 2.54.3 no frame ever reached vp8enc: a call that negotiated VP8 sent no video (framesEncoded stayed 0), or
 libwebrtc switched it to another codec. WebKit already uses LibWebRTC's own encoder for VP9 for similar reasons; use
 its libvpx VP8 encoder too (libvpx is built into libwebrtc), and offer VP8 whatever GStreamer has.
Author: LordOS <lord.basex@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-26

